                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "First of all, sorry for being excessively rough on a free cute indie game but I have no patience for this game.\n\n[h1] Places need improving: [/h1] (It'll be a no from me until these are fixed)\n[list]\n    [*]Character dialogues repeated for no reason (Seen dialogues should just appear, not repeated and I can't even fast forward the dialogue half the time. It frustrates me.)\n    [*]Translation is pretty shit.\n    [*]No clearly defined or interesting goals (Like, I'm a \"certified\" audio mixer now, I know that the bitrate of an uncompressed, CD-quality audio is 1411kbps. What the fuck do you give me?)\n[/list]\n\n[h1] My experience rant: [/h1]\nOh, you're not compatible with this bubble? That's okay, that's life, plenty other bubbles in the sea. But, it appears that you need to take tests to see your compatibility, girl. You should be able to just go to that specific bubble after you're done with one- Hm? You need to take all tests before you can pick which bubble to go for, I see... And you can't retake the test (Outside save load function but who does that)? Well, the test shouldn't be that har-\n\n*after the tests*\n3 days to prepare for the final examination, time to exercise. Exercise my fucking random facts that don't have anything to give to character or story development and go to inaccurately translated locations in the girl's PC to find unrelated lost items to give to characters I DON'T CARE ABOUT. Fucking grandpa even forgets about the girl the day after. \"What's your name little girl? ... Do you know your name means hope?\" FFS GRANDPA \n\n*after taking the final exam*\n\"So, here is your certificate.\" They're so fast with certificates these days. I can't wait to find work with this cer-\n\n*game ends, credits roll*\nWha-",
